        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "OK! I looked into it, and...\n\nThis was has never been supported! 😳\n\nUnity's input events don't respect `DefaultExecutionOrder`. Or rather, VRChat's input event do not guarantee that they'll be respected.\n\nThis issue may have been around for a long time - though let us know if it's something that only popped up recently.\n\nWe have not made any recent changes to how pickups are handled, so we expect that this issue has existed for several years.\n\nThere's a change that Unity made some internal changes that exacerbated the issue.\n\nI'm sorry that there's no easy solution!  Please let us know if you have other details! Otherwise, please resubmit this issue as a feature request.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
