  "details": "I'm working on a system to instantiate guns, however DefaultExecutionOrder is being ignored at random.\n\nI'm using InputGrab for interactions and I've attached blue cubes to visualize my hand colliders.\n\nExecution Orders:\n\n- Front Grip: -1000 (always takes priority)\n\n- Slide: -100 (takes priority over magazine)\n\n- Custom Pickup: 500\n\n- Magazine: 1000 (should always be last)\n\nVideo of it working as intended:\n\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1210269947578679388/1210269994731044925/2024-02-22_17-53-00.mp4?ex=65e9f2c4&is=65d77dc4&hm=c73d71d6768bc6549466fef885ccd4bdde771d904b8bac9f0ed6db4ee2dfe103&\n\nVideo of the bug:\n\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1210269947578679388/1210270019884290170/2024-02-22_17-51-42.mp4?ex=65e9f2ca&is=65d77dca&hm=270956e97db61b59d88f62f855de1409f9cd451a40af608587e06eeefe6c4568&\n\nThe video shows me grabbing the magazine, which shouldn't happen based on the execution order listed above. The issue seems to occurs at random.",
